{
  "help": [
    "What the detail window of the Hardware Monitor shows – tab by tab, one row per value. Saved? Close the window",
    "and open it again: the change is there at once, nothing to compile.",
    "",
    "  a value:           {\"sensor\": \"GPU Hot Spot\"}  – the name LibreHardwareMonitor gives it",
    "  * as wildcard:     {\"sensor\": \"Fan #*\"}  – all fans",
    "  type:              {\"sensor\": \"GPU Core\", \"type\": \"Clock\"}  – only if the name exists several times",
    "  own label:         {\"sensor\": \"Package\", \"text\": \"CPU total\"}  – or an id of assets\\i18n.json",
    "  leave some out:    {\"sensor\": \"CPU Core #*\", \"exclude\": \"*Distance*\"}",
    "  a group:           {\"device\": \"drive\", \"values\": [...]}  – once per device; device: cpu, gpu, ram, motherboard,",
    "                     drive, network, battery, other; \"name\": \"Intel*\" only devices of that name; \"title\": own heading",
    "  a section:         {\"section\": \"section.fans\", \"values\": [...], \"one_row\": true}  – folds shut; one_row puts",
    "                     values of the same name into one row (Fan #1: speed, then the control as a bar)",
    "  a tab of its own:  {\"title\": \"tab.power\", \"view\": \"power\"}  – power, fans, health, hardware_data, all",
    "                     (\"all\": everything LibreHardwareMonitor finds, for looking up names)",
    "",
    "What a PC does not have is simply not shown; a tab whose devices the PC has none of is hidden.",
    "explanations: [sensor type, pattern, text id] – the text in the footer when the mouse is over a value; the first",
    "whose pattern (a regular expression) matches the whole name; {0}, {1} = what its brackets caught."
  ],
  "tabs": [
    {"title": "tab.temperatures", "groups": [
      {"device": "cpu", "values": [
        {"sensor": "Core (Tctl/Tdie)"},
        {"sensor": "CCD* (Tdie)"},
        {"sensor": "CPU Package", "type": "Temperature"},
        {"sensor": "Core Max", "type": "Temperature"}
